# Data / outputs (adjust if you want to track some)
# All CSVs are ignored -- notebook-generated dataset caches (always named "diversity...") AND
# the raw aav_viability_test/aav{2,5,9}.csv source data, which is too large to track in git
# (aav5.csv alone is ~90MB) and is instead published as a GitHub Release asset -- see README
# for the download link. Derived .npy weight files (lib/aav*_{F,J}_viab_mlp.npy) are tiny and
# ARE tracked, so the repo is runnable right after a fresh clone without regenerating those.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl

# CONFIDENTIAL IDV source data -- NEVER commit, NEVER push, NEVER upload anywhere.
# Redundant with *.csv above (belt-and-suspenders): explicit named entries so the intent
# survives any future change to the *.csv rule. Real NGS read counts + enrichment for the
# AAV2/AAV5/AAV9 directed-evolution screens (viability: virus/plasmid; selectivity:
# organoid/nuclei DNA & RNA vs virus). Hundreds of MB each.
**/AAV2_organoides.csv
**/AAV5_organoides.csv
**/aav2.csv
**/aav5.csv
**/aav9.csv
**/fit4functionaav9.csv
**/*organoides*.csv

# Local technical notes -- source of truth is the notebooks + README, these PDFs/tex are
# regenerable write-ups, not tracked.
Modelization_V2/docs/

# Experimental GLM ground-truth weights (Poisson/Gamma) -- regenerable from
# AAV9_poisson_regression_GT_score_study.ipynb, not a project default GT, not tracked.
Modelization_V2/lib/aav9_*_viab_poisson.npy
Modelization_V2/lib/aav9_*_viab_gamma.npy

# AAV2/AAV5 Potts GT weights -- derived from confidential IDV organoid data, not tracked.
# (trailing * catches the _{unreg,lamX,cv} penalty tag suffix from AAV5_SEL_analysis.ipynb)
Modelization_V2/lib/aav2_*_potts*.npy
Modelization_V2/lib/aav5_*_potts*.npy

